++### Added
++
++- **`keel next --json` reports approval standing.** At an approval stage
++  (`spec_approval`, `plan_approval`, `merge_approval`) each spec's entry in
++  `keel.next/1` now carries an `approval` object: `approval.stage` (`spec`,
++  `plan` or `merge`), `approval.standing` (`absent`, `rejected` or
++  `superseded`), `approval.by` and `approval.note` naming who rejected it and
++  why (`note` is `null` when none was given), and `approval.recheck` — the
++  command that clears a rejected or superseded approval (`keel gate g0
++  <slug>`, `keel gate g1 <slug>` or `keel run <slug>`). Outside an approval
++  stage the field is omitted. Additive to `keel.next/1`.
